**js/app.js**
```js
const links = [...document.querySelectorAll('.toc a')];
const sections = links.map(a => document.querySelector(a.hash));
const spy = new IntersectionObserver(entries => {
  entries.forEach(en => {
    if (en.isIntersecting) {
      links.forEach(l => l.classList.toggle('active', l.hash === '#' + en.target.id));
    }
  });
}, { rootMargin: '-40% 0px -55% 0px' });
sections.forEach(s => spy.observe(s));
```

Why it works: the sticky TOC stays visible while the main column scrolls, and IntersectionObserver with a narrow rootMargin band marks a section active only while it crosses the upper-middle of the viewport — no scroll event math needed.

